# List tutorials (by filename without extension) that should NOT be run in automated tests.

# One entry per line. Lines starting with # are comments. Blank lines are ignored.

# Example:

# connect-third-party-llms

index
connect-third-party-llms
# review-panel-discussion now runs the panel as an orchestration `tool` node
# (draft → review → revise) rather than from inside an agent generation, so the
# original failure — a nested discussion-tool call from a generation dying with
# `fetch failed` — no longer applies. It stays ignored for a different reason:
# both agent nodes declare an `output_schema`, and the CI sandbox's
# qwen2.5:0.5b is not reliable at emitting the required structured JSON, so
# `draft`/`revise` can fail nondeterministically. Re-enable only after running
# the tutorials stack locally and confirming the run reaches `succeeded`
# repeatedly; the deterministic parts (the tool node's pause/dispatch wiring)
# are already covered by tests/smoke-tests.sh.
review-panel-discussion
# orchestrate-a-sonnet-with-workflows exercises on_enter agent dispatch, which
# runs the generation asynchronously (fire-and-forget) when a task enters a state
# and routes the outcome via on_complete. Whether the card reaches `review`
# depends on the sandbox LLM completing in time, so the forward-progress steps
# are non-deterministic in CI (same class as review-panel-discussion). The
# workflows/tasks module is covered deterministically by the server unit suite
# (rest/workflows, rest/tasks, mcp) and the smoke tests.
orchestrate-a-sonnet-with-workflows

# call-aws-and-gcp-apis-from-an-agent creates tools whose `execute.auth` signs
